            <ArticleTitle>Case of fake acute abdomen by metastatic melanoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003469X11017593</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Malignant melanoma is the neoplasm with highest probability of cardiac metastatization. Cardiac involvement by metastatic melanoma is rarely identified ante-mortem (5-30% of cases) for non-specificity of cardiac symptoms. In fact we show in this case report that abdominal pain can represent the predominant symptom. Furthermore we show the importance of linkage between clinical &amp; anamnestic data which if underestimated can lead to an improper management and to the patient exitus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
